<BaseLayout title="Privacy and cookies" description="Privacy and cookie information for the static O2AT project website.">
  <article class="narrow page-intro prose"><p class="eyebrow">Website information</p><h1>Privacy and cookies.</h1><p class="lead">The O2AT site is designed as a static technical publication.</p><h2>Data collection</h2><p>The site provides no account, contact, comment or email-subscription form. No analytics, advertising pixel or third-party embedded player is included in the site source. The RSS feed is served from this domain.</p><p>The hosting and network layer may record ordinary HTTP request data in operational access logs. Retention and access follow the operator’s host configuration. Contact the project through the public issue tracker for a specific data question; do not post personal or confidential information in a public issue.</p><h2>Cookies</h2><p>The site source sets no cookies and does not require a cookie banner. Browser storage is not used by the public pages. The Explore tools store shareable scenario parameters in the URL only when the visitor changes a scenario.</p><h2>External links</h2><p>Links to GitHub and source references leave this site. Their providers apply their own privacy terms. No third-party content is embedded automatically.</p><h2>Contact route</h2><p>For privacy questions, use the project repository’s public issue tracker and do not include sensitive data. A private contact channel is not published by this site.</p></article>
</BaseLayout>
